S1 of the rank-zero representation (619eedb6c). The run can now hold a value of rank zero:
`Array::createRankZero`, `size` taken from `numel` when there is no extent, and `__index_arr__`
refusing a rank-zero value instead of reading a dimension it has not. Print and equality already
handled rank zero, and no operator takes an open rank today, so arithmetic has no rank-zero path.
The self-test checks rank 0 / one element / size 1 / prints "1.0" / equals a 1.0 and not a 2.0.

KNOWN DEFECT, open at this commit: `func show(v: f32[..]) { println(v) }` called with a number
exits 139. One line reproduces it:

    func show(v: f32[..]) { println(v) }
    func main() { show(2.5) }

Cause: the edge from the value to the slot is not converted -- the slot of `T[..]` holds the
element itself, and the reading of that slot reads it as an array. The commit that fixes it
(S2: the wrapping conversion at the one place a value's type goes from `T` to `T[..]`, in
`Builder::coerceTo`, with the call-argument edge routed through it) must record this defect as
closed, and the gate is green until then only because no case calls a `T[..]` parameter with an
element: 7939 / 7930 / 0 with the defect live.
